Here are the MSTest patterns for each scenario:

## 1. Platform-specific tests (Windows only)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Windows")]
[System.Runtime.Versioning.SupportedOSPlatform("windows")]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows.");

    // ... registry code
}
```

## 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("RequiresGpu")]
public void Render_ProducesExpectedOutput()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") is not null)
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI — requires local GPU.");

    // ... GPU test
}
```

## 3. Retry flaky external API calls

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Flaky")]
[DataRow(1)]
[DataRow(2)]
[DataRow(3)] // poor-man's retry; see below for better option
public void Weather_ReturnsForecast(int attempt)
{
    // Not ideal — use the built-in retry attribute instead:
}

// MSTest v3.x+ supports [Retry]:
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)] // retries up to 3 times on failure
public void Weather_ReturnsForecast()
{
    var result = _weatherClient.GetForecast("Seattle");
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

> **Note:** `[Retry(n)]` is available in MSTest 3.8+. For older versions, wrap the call in a manual retry loop.

## 4. Cleanup even on failure — use `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string _tempFile = null!;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestCleanup] // runs even if the test fails or throws
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFile_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile, "data");
        var result = MyProcessor.Process(_tempFile);
        Assert.AreEqual("expected", result);
    }
}
```

For one-off cases, `try/finally` inside the test also works:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void SingleTest_CleansUp()
{
    var tmp = Path.GetTempFileName();
    try
    {
        // ... test logic
    }
    finally
    {
        File.Delete(tmp);
    }
}
```

---

**Summary table:**

| Scenario | Mechanism |
|----------|-----------|
| OS-specific | `Assert.Inconclusive()` + guard check |
| Skip in CI | Environment variable check + `Assert.Inconclusive()` |
| Flaky/retry | `[Retry(3)]` (MSTest 3.8+) |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally` |
